# Google Sheets API Configuration
# These environment variables are REQUIRED for the forms and CMS to work

# Google Sheets API Key
# Get this from: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# See API-KEY-SETUP-GUIDE.md for detailed instructions
GOOGLE_SHEETS_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SHEETS_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# Google Sheet ID
# This is the ID of your main Google Sheet (find it in the sheet URL)
# Example: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/YOUR_SHEET_ID_HERE/edit
GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=your-sheet-id-here
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=your-sheet-id-here

# Optional: Separate sheet ID for join form submissions
# If not provided, will use GOOGLE_SHEET_ID
GOOGLE_SHEETS_JOIN_FORM_ID=your-sheet-id-here

# Admin Email (optional)
# Used for notifications (if email service is configured)
ADMIN_EMAIL=info@pulsedancers.com

# IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTES:
# 
# 1. NEVER commit the actual .env file to git
#    The .env file is already in .gitignore
# 
# 2. In Vercel, add these as Environment Variables:
#    - Go to your project settings
#    - Navigate to Environment Variables
#    - Add each variable above
# 
# 3. The API key should be restricted in Google Cloud Console:
#    - Restrict to HTTP referrers (your domains only)
#    - Restrict to Google Sheets API only
#    - Set to read/write access
# 
# 4. The Google Sheet must be set to "Anyone with the link can view"
#    - Open your Google Sheet
#    - Click Share
#    - Change to "Anyone with the link"
#    - Set permission to "Viewer"
